#only("1")[#voiceover("Let's break down how the sunk cost fallacy affects financial decision-making.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("First, it causes people to focus on costs that have already been incurred, the sunk costs, rather than considering the future benefits of a decision.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("This can lead to an irrational commitment to a course of action, even when it's no longer the best choice.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("As a result, people may continue investing in losing propositions, throwing good money after bad, simply because they've already invested.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("The fallacy can also encourage risk-taking behavior in an attempt to justify past expenditures, leading to potentially more losses.")]
]

